{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["And the secret of <b>בְּזֹאת יָבֹא אַהֲרֹן אֶל הַקֹּדֶשׁ</b> (\"with this Aaron shall come into the holy place\") is like the secret of \"זֹאת אוֹת הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר הֲקִמֹתִי\" (Genesis 9:17), which I have already explained (Exodus 31:13). And our Rabbis hinted at it, for they said in Vayikra Rabbah (21:6): Rabbi Yudan interpreted the verse with reference to the High Priest — upon his entry into the Holy of Holies, bundles of mitzvot are in his hand: in the merit of the Torah — \"וְזֹאת הַתּוֹרָה\" (Deuteronomy 4:44); in the merit of circumcision — \"זֹאת בְּרִיתִי אֲשֶׁר תִּשְׁמְרוּ\" (Genesis 17:10); in the merit of Sabbath — \"אַשְׁרֵי אֱנוֹשׁ יַעֲשֶׂה זֹּאת\" (Isaiah 56:2); in the merit of Jerusalem — \"זֹאת יְרוּשָׁלַיִם\" (Ezekiel 5:5); in the merit of the tribes — \"וְזֹאת אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר לָהֶם אֲבִיהֶם\" (Genesis 49:28); in the merit of Judah — \"וְזֹאת לִיהוּדָה\" (Deuteronomy 33:7); in the merit of the Congregation of Israel — \"זֹאת קוֹמָתֵךְ דָּמְתָה לְתָמָר\" (Song of Songs 7:8); in the merit of the terumah — \"וְזֹאת הַתְּרוּמָה\" (Exodus 25:3); in the merit of the tithes — \"וּבְחָנוּנִי נָא בָּזֹאת\" (Malachi 3:10); in the merit of the sacrifices — \"בְּזֹאת יָבֹא אַהֲרֹן\". And this requires a lengthy explanation, but everything has already been clarified in our words."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:10.688391040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}